   "daf": "97a",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "מְרִיקָה כִּמְרִיקַת הַכּוֹס, שְׁטִיפָה כִּשְׁטִיפַת הַכּוֹס. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: מְרִיקָה וּשְׁטִיפָה – בְּצוֹנֵן. דִּבְרֵי רַבִּי. וַחֲכָמִים אוֹמְרִים: מְרִיקָה בְּחַמִּין, וּשְׁטִיפָה בְּצוֹנֵן.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «Scouring» is «like the scouring of a cup,» and «rinsing» is «like the rinsing of a cup;» and scouring and rinsing are both performed with cold water. «The Sages taught» in a baraita: «Scouring and rinsing» are both performed «with cold» water; this is «the statement of Rabbi» Yehuda HaNasi. «And the Rabbis say: Scouring» is performed «with hot» water, «and rinsing» is performed «with cold» water."
  }
